the back of my hand.

00:35:36.330 --> 00:35:39.007
I knew Washington DC better
than I knew Lillington."

00:35:40.520 --> 00:35:42.540
So he's talking about that.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:46.250
He says, "After a month
in service, moved,"

00:35:46.250 --> 00:35:47.610
and I wanna read some of this

00:35:47.610 --> 00:35:49.990
to give you an idea of how he wrote it.

00:35:49.990 --> 00:35:51.590
He wrote it like he was talking.

00:35:52.747 --> 00:35:53.850
"After a month in service,

00:35:53.850 --> 00:35:56.920
moved out into an apartment
behind the Iwo Jima Statue,

00:35:56.920 --> 00:35:59.070
and enjoyed it very much.

00:35:59.070 --> 00:36:00.880
Would go over to Washington Monument

00:36:00.880 --> 00:36:04.760
and run to the top several
nights a week, just for fun.

00:36:04.760 --> 00:36:08.533
It was a tough run, 897 steps to the top.

00:36:09.730 --> 00:36:12.100
We would look out when we got to the top,

00:36:12.100 --> 00:36:14.040
then run back down.

00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:16.570
The run down was much
easier than going up.

00:36:16.570 --> 00:36:19.660
I think it was longer
going up than coming down."

00:36:19.660 --> 00:36:20.493
Yep.

00:36:20.493 --> 00:36:22.280
That's a joke because
it was the same route.

00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:24.280
Right.
That was what made it funny.

00:36:24.280 --> 00:36:26.113
Yeah, yeah, I'm tracking.

00:36:27.100 --> 00:36:30.170
You gotta get a ticket to go in there now.

00:36:30.170 --> 00:36:31.710
I know, unless you're like,

00:36:31.710 --> 00:36:34.780
I guess if you're a soldier
and you have a uniform,

00:36:34.780 --> 00:36:37.280
and you have access to
drive everybody around,

00:36:37.280 --> 00:36:38.113
maybe you can just go,

00:36:38.113 --> 00:36:39.682
you have a key and you can run up there.

00:36:39.682 --> 00:36:40.515
I was just there recently,

00:36:40.515 --> 00:36:43.370
and there's a whole complex that's added

00:36:43.370 --> 00:36:45.820
to the side of one part of it

00:36:45.820 --> 00:36:48.030
where there's security
things as you go through

00:36:48.030 --> 00:36:49.280
and a little gift shop.

00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:51.900
Just think about it,
back then, it was '69,

00:36:51.900 --> 00:36:55.150
during the Vietnam War, he was running,

00:36:55.150 --> 00:36:57.550
he was driving people
around, and for exercise,

00:36:57.550 --> 00:36:59.240
running to the top of
the Washington Monument

00:36:59.240 --> 00:37:00.390
multiple nights a week.

00:37:02.410 --> 00:37:03.700
I'll never look at the Washington Monument

00:37:03.700 --> 00:37:05.253
not think of that story.

00:37:06.090 --> 00:37:09.826
Your papa-
Used to run 897 steps.

00:37:09.826 --> 00:37:10.880
And I remember he would tell us

00:37:10.880 --> 00:37:14.500
that story at some family gatherings.

00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:16.800
So it's cool that those
things made it in here

00:37:16.800 --> 00:37:20.100
and a lot more that I'm not gonna read.

00:37:20.100 --> 00:37:22.070
But he talked about,

00:37:22.070 --> 00:37:25.200
he started coaching at Cape
Fear Christian Academy.

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:27.170
And he taught the girls, taught,

00:37:27.170 --> 00:37:29.390
he coached the girls' basketball team.

00:37:29.390 --> 00:37:34.390
And they made it to the
state championship and lost.

00:37:36.070 --> 00:37:41.070
But he was a very successful
coach from the beginning,

00:37:41.150 --> 00:37:45.713
fresh out of the military and college.

00:37:47.170 --> 00:37:48.400
So he would talk about,

00:37:48.400 --> 00:37:51.080
he would tell these
stories of getting drafted,

00:37:51.080 --> 00:37:55.310
of things like that, but
it was striking sometimes

00:37:55.310 --> 00:37:59.397
